    "extracted_answer": "[150, '150^\\\\circ']",
    "gold_answer": "If $\\theta$ is the angle between the vectors, then\n\\[\\cos \\theta = \\frac{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}}{\\left\\| \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\right\\| \\left\\| \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} \\right\\|} = \\frac{(2)(-1) + (-1)(1) + (1)(0)}{\\sqrt{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{-3}{2 \\sqrt{3}} = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\]Hence, $\\theta = \\boxed{150^\\circ}.$",
